=== Prompt ===
Who is Kratos from God of War?

=== Normal Response ===
Kratos is a fictional character and the main protagonist of the God of War series, developed by Santa Monica Studio and published by Sony Interactive Entertainment. He is a Spartan warrior who serves as the main character in the God of War series, which is set in the world of Greek mythology.

Kratos is known for his immense strength, rage, and tragic past. He was originally a Spartan soldier who was tricked by the God of War, Ares, into killing his own family. This act led Kratos to become the God of War himself, but he later regretted his actions and sought redemption.

In the latest installment of the series, God of War (2018), Kratos has moved on from his past and is living in the Norse realm with his son Atreus. The game follows Kratos as he teaches Atreus about the ways of the gods and sets out on a journey to scatter the ashes of his deceased wife, Faye.

Kratos is voiced by actor Terrence C. Carson in the original God of War games, and by Christopher Judge in the 2018 reboot. He is a popular character in the gaming community and is known for his powerful combat abilities, deep backstory, and complex character development.

